basalt is an independent, clean-room work. It does not incorporate, link
against, or redistribute any NVIDIA source code, headers, libraries, or
documentation. It drives the publicly distributed `ptxas`, `nvdisasm` and
`cuobjdump` executables as external processes and records their observable
behaviour. Where it reads machine code from a distributed library, it measures
that code and stores measurements; no part of it is copied into this
repository, and none of the libraries are vendored or redistributed.

